@startuml deployment-scan-service
!include elvira.iuml
' What: two Deployments of one image share Redis db 8 and the storage volume: a bulk worker scaled 0..N by KEDA at a low PriorityClass, and one always-on interactive replica.
' Kind: UML deployment diagram. Everything here is proposed: the Ansible role lives in evilflowers-knowledge (issue to open).
' Source: issue evilflowers-scan-service#1 and its comments (2026-11-16); evilflowers-knowledge Cookbooks/Deploy-a-Service (2026-11-07)

title evilflowers-scan-service on k3s (proposed, 2026-11-16)

node "k3s (control)" {
  artifact "ghcr.io/evilflowerscatalog/evilflowers-scan-service:main" as image <<proposed>>
  node "Deployment scan\nKEDA 0..N, PriorityClass digitalizer-batch" as bulk <<proposed>> {
    component "celery worker\n--queues=evilflowers_scan.standalone" as wbulk <<focus>>
  }
  node "Deployment scan-interactive\nreplicas 1" as inter <<proposed>> {
    component "celery worker\n--queues=evilflowers_scan.standalone.interactive" as winter
  }
  database "PVC /models\n(DocRes weights)" as models <<proposed>>
  database "STORAGE_PATH volume\n(raw-scans, digitized)" as storage
  component "decider-vision\nshared namespace" as dv
  component "alloy-node :4318" as alloy
}
database "Redis db 8\n(digitalizer queues)" as redis <<proposed>>

image ..> bulk : runs
image ..> winter : runs
wbulk --> redis : consume (6379)
winter --> redis : consume (6379)
wbulk --> storage : read frames, write output_dir
winter --> storage : read frames, write output_dir
wbulk --> models : read
wbulk --> dv : HTTP /v1/systemone
winter --> dv : HTTP /v1/systemone
wbulk --> alloy : OTLP/HTTP
winter --> alloy : OTLP/HTTP

caption The bulk worker scales on the length of evilflowers_scan.standalone; the interactive replica stays up so one leaf comes back within seconds.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-scan-service · docs/diagrams/deployment-scan-service.puml
@enduml
